<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Giuliano de' Medici</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1453–1478</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Giuliano de' Medici (1453–1478) was the younger brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorenzo-de-medici">Lorenzo de' Medici</a> and a prominent figure of Florentine society, celebrated in the poetry of Poliziano. On 26 April 1478 he was stabbed to death in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence-cathedral">Florence Cathedral</a> by members of the Pazzi conspiracy, who also wounded Lorenzo. His illegitimate son Giulio was raised by Lorenzo and later became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-clement-vii">Pope Clement VII</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/giuliano-de-medici.jpg" alt="Giuliano de' Medici" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sandro Botticelli · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Botticelli,_ritratto_di_giuliano_de%27_medici_bergamo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
